    {
      "id": "hv-0",
      "conflict": "Mechanism for distributing AI productivity gains",
      "prevails": "C5",
      "criterion": "logical_validity",
      "rationale": "Accelerationist correctly identifies that taxing specific technologies creates a 'compliance moat' that favors incumbents who can afford expensive legal overhead over startups. Skeptic’s proposal lacks a mechanism to prevent capital flight or the stifling of small-scale innovation.",
      "whatWouldChange": "Empirical data showing that a specific productivity tax rate correlates with increased market competition rather than industry consolidation.",
